        "RRB exams frequently test structural differences between Monocotyledons and Dicotyledons (e.g., leaf venation, root system, cotyledon count).",
        "Identify non-vascular vs. vascular plant groups: Bryophytes lack true vascular tissue, whereas Pteridophytes are the first vascular plants.",
        "Distinguish between Gymnosperms (naked seeds) and Angiosperms (enclosed seeds in fruit) for fast conceptual questions."
